{"name":"African Safari","hex":"#b16b40","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"}],"entries":[{"title":"African Safari Airways","blocks":[{"text":"Africa Safari Airways was an airline based in Mombasa, Kenya. It operated charter flights and inclusive tours beginning in 1967 from Europe, mainly to Mombasa. Its main base was Moi International Airport, Mombasa. It ceased operations in 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/413bh_-_African_Safari_Airways_-_ASA_Airbus_A310-308%3B_5Y-VIP%40ZRH%3B09.07.2006_%288353073943%29.jpg/330px-413bh_-_African_Safari_Airways_-_ASA_Airbus_A310-308%3B_5Y-VIP%40ZRH%3B09.07.2006_%288353073943%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Safari_Airways"},{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/413bh_-_African_Safari_Airways_-_ASA_Airbus_A310-308%3B_5Y-VIP%40ZRH%3B09.07.2006_%288353073943%29.jpg/500px-413bh_-_African_Safari_Airways_-_ASA_Airbus_A310-308%3B_5Y-VIP%40ZRH%3B09.07.2006_%288353073943%29.jpg?